    "id": 6041,
    "title": "MCCKAP 2023 Question 41",
    "scenario": "A 12-year-old boy collapses during football practice. He is brought to the ICU from an urgent care center with a temperature of 38.8 °C (102 °F). A normal saline bolus of 20 mL/kg is given. His urine is dark red and urinalysis shows 10 RBCs/high-power field. His muscles are tender and his creatine kinase level is over 5,000 U/L with further results pending. The risk of acute kidney failure in this patient is most likely to be reduced by",
