    "correctAnswerText": "aggressive saline hydration.",
    "explanation": "Although diuretics and alkalization have been advocated, high-grade medical evidence is only present for aggressive saline diuresis. Animal studies suggest the benefit of alkalizing the urine, but human studies are equivocal.",
