    "displayScenario": "A 4-month-old exclusively breast-fed boy with trisomy 21 and secundum atrial septal defect presents to the emergency department with profound hypotonia. Antibiotics are initiated for presumed sepsis. Bedside echocardiography reveals mildly depressed function and mild left-to-right shunting. His chest radiograph is normal. His vital signs are: temperature 36.7 °C (98 °F), heart rate 101 beats/min, respiratory rate 26 breaths/min, blood pressure 90/47 mm Hg, and SpO2 100%. Laboratory data are summarized below. Which of the following additional tests should be performed to identify high-risk conditions for this patient?"
