    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctAnswerText": "a wave",
    "explanation": "This patient has developed a junctional rhythm as evidenced by the loss of p waves on ECG with accompanying physical findings suggesting decreased cardiac output due to loss of atrioventricular synchrony. Bypass times greater than 90 minutes and inotrope use have been associated with increased risk of junctional tachycardia. When atrioventricular synchrony is lost, such as in heart block or junctional tachycardia, the waves may be accentuated (cannon a waves) due to contraction of the atrium against a closed tricuspid valve.",
