    "id": 6122,
    "title": "MCCKAP 2023 Question 122",
    "scenario": "A 6-year-old boy is admitted with a diagnosis of respiratory failure secondary to influenza A infection complicated by bacterial pneumonia. He is endotracheally intubated and mechanically ventilated. He has been in the unit for 3 days. His mother says that he had hypothyroidism in infancy, which was treated for 6 months with levothyroxine and resolved. This morning, a thyroid panel shows: thyroid-stimulating hormone 5 mU/L, thyroxine 105 ng/dL, and triiodothyronine 70 ng/dL. These results indicate which of the following diagnoses?",
