    "correctAnswerText": "Renally dose all current medications",
    "explanation": "Fractional excretion of urea (FEUrea) = (urine urea nitrogen x serum creatinine)/(serum urea nitrogen x urine creatinine) x 100. FEUrea less than 30% indicates prerenal failure, whereas FEUrea higher than 70% indicates intrinsic renal failure. This patient's FEUrea is 92%, which suggests intrinsic renal failure. FEUrea is not altered by diuretics, whereas fractional excretion of sodium is not accurate with the use of scheduled furosemide.",
