    "displayScenario": "A 14-year-old patient admitted to the ICU with septic shock is intubated and given initial IV fluid resuscitation with normal saline solution, 60 mL/kg. A pulmonary artery catheter also is inserted. Vital signs are: temperature 102.2 °F (39 °C), heart rate 160 beats/min, and blood pressure 70/30 mm Hg. Dopamine is infused at 8 mcg/kg/min. Laboratory data are summarized below. Which of the following agents should be added at this time?",
